  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements about superheterodyne receiver:<br />\n(a) IF used in AM receiver is 455 kHz.<br />\n(b) IF used in FM receiver is 10.7 kHz.<br />\n(c) The bandwidth of IF amplifier in AM is 10 kHz.<br />\n(d) The bandwidth of IF amplifier in FM is 200 Hz.<br />\nWhich of the above statement(s) is/are correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "a"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "b"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "c"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "d"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a, c)<br />\nThe bandwidth of a single channel for an FM radio is 200 kHz. So, the bandwidth of IF amplifier<br />\nin FM is 200 kHz. Hence, option (d) is not correct.</p>"
  },
